IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 12 (the Registrar's registers, copies, certificates as evidence, refusing a document, old records)
-- and s 12A (the electronic transaction system). Layer 1 (the law, objectively). The Registrar appears only as the holder of powers and duties over the individual.
-- s 12(2)(a) and the paragraphs (a) of ss 12(2A), (2C) and (2D) are shown "[Deleted by Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]".
-- Seam (PLAN.md section 4, table A): `s 12A(1) the system is the electronic transaction system mentioned in section 12A(1)` answers the keel's input for s 4(1) "electronic transaction system".
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".

§ `Section 12(1): the Registrar keeps the registers`

-- "to keep such registers as the Registrar considers necessary": the text leaves the choice to the Registrar and is "subject to this Act" (other sections require particular registers),
-- so a register the Registrar does not consider necessary is not answered here (fork line F-H-D1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2805 | 12.—(1) The Registrar is, subject to this Act, to keep such registers
-- src:2806 | as the Registrar considers necessary in such form as he or she thinks
-- src:2807 | fit.
@ref s 12(1) (src:2805-2807)
GIVEN `the Registrar considers the register necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) the Registrar is to keep the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar considers the register necessary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such registers as the Registrar considers necessary", "subject to this Act"; the text says nothing of a register the Registrar does not consider necessary

§ `Section 12(2): any person may require a copy, or have access to a register, on payment of the prescribed fee`

-- (2)(b): subject to (2AA), a copy of the notice of incorporation, any certificate issued under this Act, any document or extract kept by the Registrar, to be given or certified.
-- The exclusions are the text's own "does not apply": (2AB) a prescribed excluded document; (2AC) the entries a form on the electronic transaction system excludes;
-- (2A) a specified exempt private company wholly owned by the Government; (2B) a document or certificate filed, lodged or issued before the cancellation of such a notification.
-- "on payment of the prescribed fee": a grant gated by a payment, not by "if", "where" or "upon": NOTHING when it is not paid (fork line F-H-S3).
-- src:2809 | (2) Any person may, on payment of the prescribed fee —
-- src:2813 | (b) subject to subsection (2AA), require a copy of the notice of
-- src:2814 | incorporation of a company, any certificate issued under
-- src:2815 | this Act, any document or extract from any document kept
-- src:2816 | by the Registrar to be given or certified by the Registrar;
@ref s 12(2)(b) (src:2809-2816)
GIVEN `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is for a copy of the notice of incorporation of a company, a certificate issued under this Act, or a document or an extract from a document kept by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is prescribed as an excluded document for the purposes of subsection (2AB)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is for an entry that subsection (2AC) excludes from the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is one that the Minister has specified under subsection (2A), and the notification has not been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled, and the document or certificate was filed, lodged or issued before the date of the cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(b) the person may require a copy of the document or certificate, or an extract, to be given or certified by the Registrar` MEANS
    IF    `the document is prescribed as an excluded document for the purposes of subsection (2AB)`
       OR `the request is for an entry that subsection (2AC) excludes from the document`
       OR `the company is one that the Minister has specified under subsection (2A), and the notification has not been cancelled`
       OR `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled, and the document or certificate was filed, lodged or issued before the date of the cancellation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2)(b) does not apply to any document prescribed as an excluded document" (2AB); "the references to the document in subsection (2)(b) exclude the following entries" (2AC); "Subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to such exempt private company" (2A); "subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to any document or certificate relating to that company that is filed or lodged ... before the date of such cancellation" (2B) (flat negatives)
    ELSE (IF `the request is for a copy of the notice of incorporation of a company, a certificate issued under this Act, or a document or an extract from a document kept by the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `the prescribed fee has been paid`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant "on payment of the prescribed fee"; the fee is not paid; the text says nothing of a person who has not paid (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S3)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is to a copy of the notice of incorporation, a certificate issued under this Act, or a document or extract kept by the Registrar; the text says nothing of any other thing

-- src:2809 | (2) Any person may, on payment of the prescribed fee —
-- src:2821 | (c) have access to any register of directors, chief executive
-- src:2822 | officers, secretaries or auditors of a company kept by the
-- src:2823 | Registrar under section 173(1) by obtaining a copy of or an
-- src:2824 | extract from it; or
@ref s 12(2)(c) (src:2809-2824)
GIVEN `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is a register of directors, chief executive officers, secretaries or auditors of a company kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(c) the person may have access to the register by obtaining a copy of or an extract from it` MEANS
    IF `the register is a register of directors, chief executive officers, secretaries or auditors of a company kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)`
    THEN (IF `the prescribed fee has been paid`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant "on payment of the prescribed fee"; the fee is not paid (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S3)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the registers kept under section 173(1)

-- src:2809 | (2) Any person may, on payment of the prescribed fee —
-- src:2828 | (d) have access to the electronic register of members of a
-- src:2829 | private company kept by the Registrar under section 196A
-- src:2830 | by obtaining a copy of or an extract from it.
@ref s 12(2)(d) (src:2809-2830)
GIVEN `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is one that the Minister has specified under subsection (2A), and the notification has not been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled, and the document or certificate was filed, lodged or issued before the date of the cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(d) the person may have access to the electronic register of members by obtaining a copy of or an extract from it` MEANS
    IF `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company kept by the Registrar under section 196A`
    THEN (IF    `the company is one that the Minister has specified under subsection (2A), and the notification has not been cancelled`
             OR `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled, and the document or certificate was filed, lodged or issued before the date of the cancellation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to such exempt private company that is wholly owned by the Government as the Minister may ... specify" (2A) and "subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to any document or certificate relating to that company" (2B) (flat negatives)
          ELSE (IF `the prescribed fee has been paid`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant "on payment of the prescribed fee"; the fee is not paid (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S3)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the electronic register of members of a private company kept under section 196A

§ `Section 12(2AA) to (2D): the certificate of confirmation, excluded documents, and copies without charge`

-- (2AA) "may only be issued to the company upon an application made in accordance with those provisions": "only" closes the gate, so JUST FALSE without an application (grant ruling, limit 2).
-- src:2836 | (2AA) A certificate of confirmation of incorporation mentioned in
-- src:2837 | section 17(9) or 19(7) may only be issued to the company upon an
-- src:2838 | application made in accordance with those provisions.
@ref s 12(2AA) (src:2836-2838)
GIVEN `an application was made in accordance with section 17(9) or 19(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2AA) the certificate of confirmation of incorporation may be issued to the company` MEANS
    IF `an application was made in accordance with section 17(9) or 19(7)`
    THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says the certificate "may only be issued ... upon an application"; it grants no right to one where an application was made (that is sections 17(9) and 19(7))
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A certificate of confirmation of incorporation mentioned in section 17(9) or 19(7) may only be issued to the company upon an application made in accordance with those provisions" (a closed gate: "only")

-- src:2842 | (2AB) Subsection (2)(b) does not apply to any document prescribed
-- src:2843 | as an excluded document for the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 12(2AB) (src:2842-2843)
GIVEN `the document is prescribed as an excluded document for the purposes of subsection (2AB)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2AB) subsection (2)(b) applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is prescribed as an excluded document for the purposes of subsection (2AB)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2)(b) does not apply to any document prescribed as an excluded document for the purposes of this subsection" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a document prescribed as excluded; the prescription is outside the sources

DECLARE `s 12(2AC) entry` IS ONE OF
    `s 12(2AC)(a) a means of notification provided by a person for the purposes of section 28A(1)(b) of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004`
    `s 12(2AC)(b) an individual's date of birth obtained under this Act or section 28(1A) of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004`
    `s 12(2AC)(c) any other prescribed information`
    `s 12(2AC) any other entry`

-- "Where a document is submitted on or after the date of commencement of section 28 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 using a form on the electronic transaction system":
-- the commencement date is in another Act and not among the sources, so whether the document was submitted on or after it is a fact the person states.
-- src:2849 | (2AC) Where a document is submitted on or after the date of
-- src:2850 | commencement of section 28 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory
-- src:2851 | Enhancements) Act 2024 using a form on the electronic transaction
-- src:2852 | system, the references to the document in subsection (2)(b) exclude
-- src:2853 | the following entries in the form:
-- src:2855 | (a) a means of notification provided by a person for the
-- src:2856 | purposes of section 28A(1)(b) of the Accounting and
-- src:2857 | Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004;
-- src:2859 | (b) an individual’s date of birth obtained under this Act or
-- src:2860 | section 28(1A) of the Accounting and Corporate
-- src:2861 | Regulatory Authority Act 2004;
-- src:2863 | (c) any other prescribed information.
@ref s 12(2AC) (src:2849-2863)
GIVEN `the document was submitted on or after the date of commencement of section 28 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 using a form on the electronic transaction system` IS A BOOLEAN
      entry IS A `s 12(2AC) entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2AC) the entry is excluded from the document for the purposes of subsection (2)(b)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document was submitted on or after the date of commencement of section 28 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 using a form on the electronic transaction system`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document is submitted on or after the date of commencement of section 28 ... using a form on the electronic transaction system, the references to the document in subsection (2)(b) exclude the following entries" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
    ELSE (CONSIDER entry
          WHEN `s 12(2AC)(a) a means of notification provided by a person for the purposes of section 28A(1)(b) of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 12(2AC)(b) an individual's date of birth obtained under this Act or section 28(1A) of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 12(2AC)(c) any other prescribed information` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "exclude the following entries" lists three without "only"; the text says nothing of any other entry

-- (2A): "Subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to such exempt private company that is wholly owned by the Government as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, specify where the Minister
-- considers that it would not be in the public interest for ... any certificate or copy of or extract from any document relating to any such company to be given or certified to any member of the public."
-- src:2869 | (2A) Subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to such exempt
-- src:2870 | private company that is wholly owned by the Government as the
-- src:2871 | Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, specify where the
-- src:2872 | Minister considers that it would not be in the public interest for —
-- src:2879 | (b) any certificate or copy of or extract from any document
-- src:2880 | relating to any such company to be given or certified to any
-- src:2881 | member of the public.
@ref s 12(2A) (src:2869-2881)
GIVEN `the company is an exempt private company that is wholly owned by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has specified the company by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers that it would not be in the public interest for a certificate or copy of or extract from a document relating to the company to be given or certified to a member of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2A) subsection (2)(b) and (d) does not apply to the company` MEANS
    IF    `the company is an exempt private company that is wholly owned by the Government`
      AND `the Minister has specified the company by notification in the Gazette`
      AND `the Minister considers that it would not be in the public interest for a certificate or copy of or extract from a document relating to the company to be given or certified to a member of the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exclusion reaches only "such exempt private company ... as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, specify"; the notification is outside the sources, and the text says nothing of a company the Minister has not specified

-- src:2887 | (2B) Despite the cancellation of any notification mentioned in
-- src:2888 | subsection (2A) in respect of a company, subsection (2)(b) and (d)
-- src:2889 | does not apply to any document or certificate relating to that company
-- src:2890 | that is filed or lodged with the Registrar, or issued under the Act,
-- src:2891 | before the date of such cancellation, whether or not that company
-- src:2892 | remains an exempt private company wholly owned by the
-- src:2893 | Government, and whether or not it has been wound up.
@ref s 12(2B) (src:2887-2893)
GIVEN `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or certificate was filed or lodged with the Registrar, or issued under the Act, before the date of the cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2B) subsection (2)(b) and (d) continues not to apply to the document or certificate` MEANS
    IF `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled` AND `the document or certificate was filed or lodged with the Registrar, or issued under the Act, before the date of the cancellation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite the cancellation ... does not apply to any document or certificate ... filed or lodged ... or issued ... before the date of such cancellation"; the text says nothing of a document filed or issued after it (it is then subject to (2) as it stands)

-- src:2899 | (2C) Despite subsection (2), a director, chief executive officer,
-- src:2900 | secretary, auditor or member of a company may, without charge —
-- src:2902 | (a) [Deleted by Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]
-- src:2904 | (b) obtain from the Registrar a copy of or an extract from the
-- src:2905 | register of directors, register of chief executive officers,
-- src:2906 | register of secretaries and register of auditors of that
-- src:2907 | company kept by the Registrar under section 173(1).
@ref s 12(2C) (src:2899-2907)
GIVEN `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary, auditor or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy or extract is of the register of directors, register of chief executive officers, register of secretaries or register of auditors of that company kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2C) the person may obtain the copy or extract from the Registrar without charge` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary, auditor or member of the company` AND `the copy or extract is of the register of directors, register of chief executive officers, register of secretaries or register of auditors of that company kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite subsection (2), a director, chief executive officer, secretary, auditor or member of a company may, without charge ... obtain from the Registrar a copy of or an extract from the register ... of that company"; the text says nothing of another person or another register

-- src:2911 | (2D) Despite subsection (2), a director, chief executive officer,
-- src:2912 | secretary, auditor or member of a private company may, without
-- src:2913 | charge —
-- src:2915 | (a) [Deleted by Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]
-- src:2917 | (b) obtain from the Registrar a copy of or an extract from the
-- src:2918 | register of members of that company kept by the Registrar
-- src:2919 | under section 196A.
@ref s 12(2D) (src:2911-2919)
GIVEN `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary, auditor or member of the private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy or extract is of the register of members of that company kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2D) the person may obtain the copy or extract of the register of members from the Registrar without charge` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary, auditor or member of the private company` AND `the copy or extract is of the register of members of that company kept by the Registrar under section 196A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite subsection (2), a director, chief executive officer, secretary, auditor or member of a private company may, without charge ... obtain from the Registrar a copy of or an extract from the register of members of that company"; the text says nothing of another person or another register

§ `Section 12(3) to (7): certified copies and certificates as evidence, refusing a document, old records`

-- src:2925 | (3) A copy of or an extract from any document (including a copy
-- src:2926 | produced by way of microfilm) filed or lodged with the Registrar
-- src:2927 | using a non‑electronic medium that is certified to be a true copy or
-- src:2932 | extract by the Registrar is in any proceedings admissible in evidence
-- src:2933 | as of equal validity with the original document.
@ref s 12(3) (src:2925-2933)
GIVEN `the document was filed or lodged with the Registrar using a non-electronic medium` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy or extract (including a copy produced by way of microfilm) is certified by the Registrar to be a true copy or extract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(3) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as of equal validity with the original document` MEANS
    IF `the document was filed or lodged with the Registrar using a non-electronic medium` AND `the copy or extract (including a copy produced by way of microfilm) is certified by the Registrar to be a true copy or extract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a document "filed or lodged with the Registrar using a non-electronic medium" and a copy "certified to be a true copy or extract by the Registrar"; it says nothing of any other copy

-- src:2939 | (4) In any legal proceedings, a certificate issued by the Registrar
-- src:2940 | that a requirement of this Act specified in the certificate —
-- src:2942 | (a) had or had not been complied with at a date or within a
-- src:2943 | period specified in the certificate; or
-- src:2945 | (b) had been complied with upon a date specified in the
-- src:2946 | certificate but not before that date,
-- src:2948 | shall be received as prima facie evidence of the matters specified in
-- src:2949 | the certificate.
@ref s 12(4) (src:2939-2949)
GIVEN `the proceedings are legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate was issued by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that a requirement of this Act specified in it had or had not been complied with at a date or within a period specified in it, or had been complied with upon a date specified in it but not before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(4) the certificate is to be received as prima facie evidence of the matters specified in it` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are legal proceedings` AND `the certificate was issued by the Registrar` AND `the certificate states that a requirement of this Act specified in it had or had not been complied with at a date or within a period specified in it, or had been complied with upon a date specified in it but not before that date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a certificate issued by the Registrar that a requirement of this Act specified in the certificate (a) had or had not been complied with ... or (b) had been complied with upon a date ... but not before that date" in legal proceedings; it says nothing of any other certificate

-- (5): "If the Registrar is of the opinion that any document submitted to him or her -- (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..., he or she may refuse to register or receive the document":
-- a grant gated by "If": NOTHING when no limb holds (grant ruling, limit 1; fork line F-H-S3).
-- src:2955 | (5) If the Registrar is of the opinion that any document submitted to
-- src:2956 | him or her —
-- src:2958 | (a) contains any matter contrary to law;
-- src:2960 | (b) by reason of any omission or misdescription has not been
-- src:2961 | duly completed;
-- src:2963 | (c) does not comply with the requirements of this Act; or
-- src:2965 | (d) contains any error, alteration or erasure,
-- src:2967 | he or she may refuse to register or receive the document and request
-- src:2968 | that the document be appropriately amended or completed and
-- src:2969 | resubmitted or that a fresh document be submitted in its place.
@ref s 12(5) (src:2955-2969)
GIVEN `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document contains any matter contrary to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document has not been duly completed by reason of an omission or misdescription` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document contains an error, alteration or erasure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(5) the Registrar may refuse to register or receive the document and request that it be amended or completed and resubmitted, or that a fresh document be submitted in its place` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document contains any matter contrary to law`
       OR `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document has not been duly completed by reason of an omission or misdescription`
       OR `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document does not comply with the requirements of this Act`
       OR `the Registrar is of the opinion that the document contains an error, alteration or erasure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("he or she may refuse") whose "If" gate is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3)

DECLARE `s 12(6) route` IS ONE OF
    `s 12(6)(a) destroy the document with the authorisation of the National Library Board under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995`
    `s 12(6)(b) transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore under section 16 of that Act`

-- src:2973 | (6) If the Registrar is of the opinion that it is no longer necessary or
-- src:2974 | desirable to retain any document lodged, filed or registered with the
-- src:2975 | Registrar and which has been microfilmed or converted to electronic
-- src:2976 | form, the Registrar may —
-- src:2981 | (a) destroy the document with the authorisation of the
-- src:2982 | National Library Board under section 17 of the National
-- src:2983 | Library Board Act 1995; or
-- src:2985 | (b) transfer the document to the National Archives of
-- src:2986 | Singapore under section 16 of that Act.
@ref s 12(6) (src:2973-2986)
GIVEN route IS A `s 12(6) route`
      `the Registrar is of the opinion that it is no longer necessary or desirable to retain the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document has been microfilmed or converted to electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the National Library Board has authorised the destruction under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(6) the Registrar may destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is of the opinion that it is no longer necessary or desirable to retain the document`
      AND `the document has been microfilmed or converted to electronic form`
      AND (CONSIDER route
           WHEN `s 12(6)(a) destroy the document with the authorisation of the National Library Board under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995` THEN `the National Library Board has authorised the destruction under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995`
           WHEN `s 12(6)(b) transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore under section 16 of that Act` THEN TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the Registrar may") whose "If" gate is not met, or whose route (a) lacks "the authorisation of the National Library Board"; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3)

-- src:2990 | (7) In subsection (3), “non‑electronic medium” means a medium
-- src:2991 | other than the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A
-- src:2992 | of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004.
@ref s 12(7) (src:2990-2992)
GIVEN `the medium is the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(7) the medium is a non-electronic medium` MEANS
    IF `the medium is the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'non-electronic medium' means a medium other than the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004" (a "means" definition)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 12A: the electronic transaction system`

-- src:2998 | 12A.—(1) The Registrar may —
-- src:3000 | (a) require or permit any person to carry out any transaction
-- src:3001 | with the Registrar under this Act; and
-- src:3003 | (b) issue any approval, certificate, notice, determination or
-- src:3004 | other document pursuant or connected to a transaction
-- src:3005 | mentioned in paragraph (a),
-- src:3007 | using the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of
-- src:3008 | the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004.
@ref s 12A(1) (src:2998-3008)
GIVEN `the system is the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(1) the system is the electronic transaction system mentioned in section 12A(1)` MEANS
    IF `the system is the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names one system, "the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004", and says nothing of any other

-- src:2998 | 12A.—(1) The Registrar may —
-- src:3000 | (a) require or permit any person to carry out any transaction
-- src:3001 | with the Registrar under this Act; and
-- src:3007 | using the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of
-- src:3008 | the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004.
@ref s 12A(1)(a) (src:2998-3008)
GIVEN `the act is a transaction with the Registrar under this Act, as subsection (4) uses the word` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(1)(a) the Registrar may require or permit the person to carry out the transaction using the electronic transaction system` MEANS
    IF `the act is a transaction with the Registrar under this Act, as subsection (4) uses the word`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any transaction with the Registrar under this Act"; the text says nothing of any other act

-- src:2998 | 12A.—(1) The Registrar may —
-- src:3003 | (b) issue any approval, certificate, notice, determination or
-- src:3004 | other document pursuant or connected to a transaction
-- src:3005 | mentioned in paragraph (a),
-- src:3007 | using the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of
-- src:3008 | the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004.
@ref s 12A(1)(b) (src:2998-3008)
GIVEN `the document is an approval, certificate, notice, determination or other document pursuant or connected to a transaction mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(1)(b) the Registrar may issue the document using the electronic transaction system` MEANS
    IF `the document is an approval, certificate, notice, determination or other document pursuant or connected to a transaction mentioned in paragraph (a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to issue a document "pursuant or connected to a transaction mentioned in paragraph (a)"; the text says nothing of any other document

-- (2): "If the Registrar is satisfied that a transaction should be treated as having been carried out at some date and time earlier ..., the Registrar may cause the electronic transaction system and the registers ... to reflect such earlier date and time."
-- src:3012 | (2) If the Registrar is satisfied that a transaction should be treated as
-- src:3013 | having been carried out at some date and time earlier than the date and
-- src:3014 | time which is reflected in the electronic transaction system, the
-- src:3015 | Registrar may cause the electronic transaction system and the
-- src:3016 | registers kept by the Registrar to reflect such earlier date and time.
@ref s 12A(2) (src:3012-3016)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the transaction should be treated as having been carried out at some date and time earlier than the date and time reflected in the electronic transaction system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(2) the Registrar may cause the electronic transaction system and the registers to reflect the earlier date and time` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the transaction should be treated as having been carried out at some date and time earlier than the date and time reflected in the electronic transaction system`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the Registrar may") whose "If" gate is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3)

-- (3): "The Registrar must keep a record whenever the electronic transaction system or the registers are altered under subsection (2)": a duty gated by "whenever" (counts as "where": delegated-defences ruling (c)).
-- src:3020 | (3) The Registrar must keep a record whenever the electronic
-- src:3021 | transaction system or the registers are altered under subsection (2).
@ref s 12A(3) (src:3020-3021)
GIVEN `the electronic transaction system or the registers were altered under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(3) the Registrar must keep a record of the alteration` MEANS
    IF `the electronic transaction system or the registers were altered under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must keep a record whenever the electronic transaction system or the registers are altered under subsection (2)" (a failed "whenever": counts as "where", the delegated-defences ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); a duty's own question)

DECLARE `s 12A(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 12A(3) keep a record of the alteration of the electronic transaction system or the registers under subsection (2)`

-- A MUST with no time limit and no consequence the text states: no breach path (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:3020 | (3) The Registrar must keep a record whenever the electronic
-- src:3021 | transaction system or the registers are altered under subsection (2).
@ref s 12A(3) (src:3020-3021)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12A(3) act`
`s 12A(3) the Registrar must keep a record whenever the system or the registers are altered under subsection (2)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12A(3) keep a record of the alteration of the electronic transaction system or the registers under subsection (2)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12A(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not keep a record of an alteration of the electronic transaction system or the registers under subsection (2)" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:3025 | (4) In this section —
-- src:3027 | “document” includes any application, form, report, certification,
-- src:3028 | notice, confirmation, declaration, return or other document
-- src:3029 | (whether in electronic form or otherwise) filed or lodged
-- src:3030 | with, or submitted to, the Registrar;
@ref s 12A(4) (src:3025-3030)
GIVEN `the thing is an application, form, report, certification, notice, confirmation, declaration, return or other document (whether in electronic form or otherwise) filed or lodged with, or submitted to, the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(4) "document" the thing is a document` MEANS
    IF `the thing is an application, form, report, certification, notice, confirmation, declaration, return or other document (whether in electronic form or otherwise) filed or lodged with, or submitted to, the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "'document' includes any application, form, report ... filed or lodged with, or submitted to, the Registrar" leaves the term open

-- src:3035 | “transaction”, in relation to the Registrar, means —
-- src:3037 | (a) the filing or lodging of any document with the
-- src:3038 | Registrar, or the submission, production, delivery,
-- src:3039 | furnishing or sending of any document to the
-- src:3040 | Registrar;
-- src:3042 | (b) any making of any application, submission or request
-- src:3043 | to the Registrar;
-- src:3045 | (c) any provision of any undertaking or declaration to the
-- src:3046 | Registrar; and
-- src:3048 | (d) any extraction, retrieval or accessing of any
-- src:3049 | document, record or information maintained by the
-- src:3050 | Registrar.
@ref s 12A(4) (src:3035-3050)
GIVEN `the act is the filing or lodging of a document with the Registrar, or the submission, production, delivery, furnishing or sending of a document to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the making of an application, submission or request to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the provision of an undertaking or declaration to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the extraction, retrieval or accessing of a document, record or information maintained by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12A(4) "transaction" the act is a transaction in relation to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF    `the act is the filing or lodging of a document with the Registrar, or the submission, production, delivery, furnishing or sending of a document to the Registrar`
       OR `the act is the making of an application, submission or request to the Registrar`
       OR `the act is the provision of an undertaking or declaration to the Registrar`
       OR `the act is the extraction, retrieval or accessing of a document, record or information maintained by the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'transaction', in relation to the Registrar, means -- (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." (a "means" definition)
